From 7ec992f92cf3e8cd984a39b4a0e176be5f4e3a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:18:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 028/468] UPSTREAM: riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2044: Add Zic64b ISA
 extension

The SG2044 cores have 64-byte cache blocks, described by their
cbom/cbop/cboz-block-size of 64, so they implement Zic64b.  Declare it in
each core's riscv,isa-extensions.

Acked-by: Inochi Amaoto <inochiama@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Guodong Xu <guodong.xu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260920-rva23u64-hwprobe-v2-v8-7-5f14bc5c23d3@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Paul Walmsley <pjw@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit ca0c312bdf6a1dd20ac2f5da1d0760b7925da4f3)
Signed-off-by: Han Gao <gaohan@iscas.ac.cn>
